            <header class="lesson-header"><span class="lesson-number">Lesson 6</span><h1>Dependency Injection</h1><div class="lesson-meta"><span class="lesson-duration"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/></svg>30 min</span><span class="lesson-level intermediate">Intermediate</span></div></header>
            <div class="lesson-body">
                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>What is Dependency Injection?</h2>
                    <p>Dependency Injection (DI) is a design pattern that helps create loosely coupled, testable code. Instead of creating dependencies directly, they're "injected" from outside.</p>
                </section>
                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Service Lifetimes</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// Transient: New instance every time
builder.Services.AddTransient&lt;IEmailService, EmailService&gt;();

// Scoped: One instance per HTTP request
builder.Services.AddScoped&lt;IProductRepository, ProductRepository&gt;();

// Singleton: One instance for the entire application lifetime
builder.Services.AddSingleton&lt;ICacheService, CacheService&gt;();</code></pre>
                    <div class="info-box"><div class="info-box-header"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12" y2="12"/><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12.01" y2="8"/></svg><span>When to Use Each</span></div><ul><li><strong>Transient:</strong> Lightweight, stateless services</li><li><strong>Scoped:</strong> Database contexts, repositories (most common)</li><li><strong>Singleton:</strong> Configuration, caching, HTTP clients</li></ul></div>
                </section>
                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Registering Services</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// Program.cs
var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);

// Register your services
builder.Services.AddScoped&lt;IProductRepository, ProductRepository&gt;();
builder.Services.AddScoped&lt;IProductService, ProductService&gt;();
builder.Services.AddSingleton&lt;ICacheService, MemoryCacheService&gt;();

// Register DbContext
builder.Services.AddDbContext&lt;AppDbContext&gt;(options =>
    options.UseSqlServer(builder.Configuration.GetConnectionString("Default")));

// Register HttpClient
builder.Services.AddHttpClient&lt;IExternalApiService, ExternalApiService&gt;();</code></pre>
                </section>
                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Constructor Injection</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">public class ProductsController : ControllerBase
{
    private readonly IProductService _productService;
    private readonly ILogger&lt;ProductsController&gt; _logger;

    public ProductsController(
        IProductService productService,
        ILogger&lt;ProductsController&gt; logger)
    {
        _productService = productService;
        _logger = logger;
    }

    [HttpGet]
    public async Task&lt;ActionResult&lt;IEnumerable&lt;Product&gt;&gt;&gt; GetAll()
    {
        _logger.LogInformation("Getting all products");
        return Ok(await _productService.GetAllAsync());
    }
}</code></pre>
                </section>
                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Key Takeaways</h2>
                    <div class="takeaways">
                        <div class="takeaway"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg><span>DI is built into ASP.NET Core—no external library needed.</span></div>
                        <div class="takeaway"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg><span>Choose the right lifetime: Transient, Scoped, or Singleton.</span></div>
                        <div class="takeaway"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg><span>Use Scoped for most services, especially those using DbContext.</span></div>
                        <div class="takeaway"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg><span>Inject interfaces, not concrete types, for testability.</span></div>
                    </div>
                </section>
